    "created_at": "2016-10-31T10:32:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-31T10:32:08Z",
    "body": "Didn't have to look too far, https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=25412 has a Live DOM case used to determine current behavior.\n\nI don't have much of an opinion on what behavior makes sense. Is there a recursion check for other cases where a script can call into C++ which synchronously invokes a callback? For dispatchEvent it looks like the limit varies quite a bit: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4628\n\nLooks like an explicit test for the Gecko behavior should be easier than a test for its absence, does a test already exist in the Gecko tree that you could upstream to web-platform-tests?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
